1	//! The `squash-push` subcommand: squash the working copy into its
2	//! parent, advance a bookmark, and push: capture a repo's trailing
3	//! writes and publish them in one step.
4	//!
5	//! - Built for the bot's `.claude` bot repo, whose working copy
6	//!   accumulates session data continuously (the session tail). Also
7	//!   useful on the work repo as a deliberate amend-and-push (a
8	//!   published-history rewrite, so the push is a forced update).
9	//! - Runs synchronously: preflight validations, then squash +
10	//!   bookmark-set + push. A failure is a visible non-zero exit
11	//!   (the retired 0.69.0-2 predecessor delegated to a detached
12	//!   child that a sandboxed run silently killed: the loss
13	//!   diagnosed in 0.68.1).
14	//! - Prechecks and after-checks with one verdict: the working copy
15	//!   and the bookmark's publish state from `status`, plus this
16	//!   command's own question of whether the bookmark has reached the
17	//!   squash target. A run with nothing to do prints `<label>: clean`
18	//!   and stops, and every other run prints the line again after the
19	//!   push. The after-check reports only, since the exit code is the
20	//!   push's.
21	//! - Reports an at-rest publish mismatch (BOOKMARK not matching
22	//!   `BOOKMARK@origin`, an earlier publish was lost) and proceeds:
23	//!   publishing is the command's job, so healing is not
24	//!   auto-fixing. Suppressed when run as push's `squash-push-bot`
25	//!   stage, where the mismatch is the normal mid-push state.
26	
